-- the key type keeps the zone it was created with (otherwise every arm below is a tautology)
UTC

-- monotonic chain over a zone-less key, equality and range
1	1
1	1

-- the same key through a Nullable wrapper
1	1

-- a timezone-sensitive non-monotonic key: the pruner must look for the key value computed in
-- the frozen zone (hour 20 in UTC), because that is the zone the stored values were computed in
1	1
Condition: (dt in [\'1704225600\', \'1704225600\'])
Condition: (cityHash64(toHour(dt)) in [1626306447464072420, 1626306447464072420])
Condition: true
1626306447464072420

-- a single CAST as the whole key expression
1	1

-- pruning is still active: the matching literal reads one part of two, a non-matching one none
Condition: (dt in [\'1704225600\', \'1704225600\'])
Parts: 1/2
Condition: (toYYYYMMDD(dt) in [20240102, 20240102])
Parts: 1/1
Condition: true
Parts: 1/1
Condition: (dt in [\'1706731200\', \'1706731200\'])
Parts: 0/2
Condition: (toYYYYMMDD(dt) in [20240131, 20240131])
Parts: 0/0
Condition: true
Parts: 0/0

-- negative control: a type that names its zone keeps parsing in it, whatever the session says
1	1

-- negative control: a constant that is not text is not parsed, so it keeps its own zone
1	1

-- negative control: a key whose CAST input is not a DateTime still takes the direct fast path,
-- which is what makes granule pruning possible for a round trip that cannot be done safely
1	1
Granules: 1/2
